<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Database>
    <EnglishText>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10105A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>There Can Be Only One</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10105A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The horseman Genghis Khan strikes Alexander as an odious and arrogant man. His cavalry maraud across the landscape as if it belongs to them. Admittedly, their horses are purebred and quick - a shame the riders are barbarians.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10106B_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>There Can Be Only One</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10106B_NAME">
            <Text>Put him in his place.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10106B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Highest Level Commander Receives the Shock Tactics promotion (or receives enough Experience to gain a level)</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10106B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>This world has room for only one conqueror.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10106B_IMPERATIVE">
            <Text>Conquer a Settlement from Genghis Khan.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10105C_NAME">
            <Text>Horses can serve any master.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10105C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10107A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Blind Bard</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10107A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Wine flows at a banquet as {1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} thinkers discuss recent advancements in writing. One scholar suggests it could be a form for recording stories of {2_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} heroes or even of Alexander. A blind bard sings from the corner, a smile turning his lips.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10107B_NAME">
            <Text>Bring a writer on future campaigns.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10107B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10107C_NAME">
            <Text>Writing is a tool for merchants.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10107C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10107D_NAME">
            <Text>Commission a copy of the bard's tale.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10107D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10108A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>A Lifting of Spirits</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10108A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>It has been a grueling campaign, and Alexander’s army seems ready to mutiny at any moment. Over the course of the war, many local women have joined the camp, yet battle has left no room for celebration. Perhaps a night of levity will cure their war-weary spirits.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10108B_NAME">
            <Text>Marry everyone who wishes. Open the casks!</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10108B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10108C_NAME">
            <Text>They have waited this long. Continue the march.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10108C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on Cavalry Units, but 33 Damage to all Cavalry Units.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10109A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Companions</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10109A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Swift steeds and shining bronze mark the Hetairoi as they charge across the battlefield, wreaking havoc on enemy lines. {1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} horses are of exceptional stock, worthy of the elite warriors who ride them. No other general can claim such a loyal force.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10109B_NAME">
            <Text>A man’s horse is his closest companion.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10109B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>+5 Healing on Cavalry Units.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10109C_NAME">
            <Text>Only ride with men you trust.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10109C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on all Current Commanders.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10110A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>An Unusual Aegis</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10110A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Rumors swirl that Alexander cannot be harmed. Battle after battle, he avoids lethal blows and quickly recovers from any injury. The eyes of the Gorgon on his shield glisten as if alive. The men eagerly await the next fight, though some eye the Gorgon from a distance.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10110B_NAME">
            <Text>Such a divine gift marks a true hero.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10110B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10110C_NAME">
            <Text>Offer sacrifices for more good fortune.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10110C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on Cavalry Units.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10111A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The End of Hellas</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10111A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The last of the old Greek settlements has fallen. Her philosophers and her countrymen now answer to Alexander; her people are lost in the sea of {1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} faces. All things end in time, yet the world seems to sigh at what might have been.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10111B_NAME">
            <Text>Hellas will be the new heart of the realm.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10111B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_STORY_CITY} becomes your Capital and Unrest is removed. {2_Capital} becomes a City if allowed.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10111C_NAME">
            <Text>Marble can be repurposed for {1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} needs.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10111C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10111D_NAME">
            <Text>Integrate the Greeks into the army.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10111D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>+1 Tier 2 Hoplite in {1_STORY_CITY}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10112A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>From One Phalanx to Another</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10112A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The long sarissas of Alexander’s phalanxes may look unwieldy to an outsider, but even the famed Greek hoplite falls before its reach. Their long shields cannot withstand the pressure of rows of pikes, and even Greeks feel fear.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10112B_NAME">
            <Text>Little will be lost when the Greeks fall.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10112B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on Infantry Units.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10112C_NAME">
            <Text>Their poetry is worth saving at least.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10112C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10113A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>On Kingship</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10113A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The King and his teacher walk the paths of the Acropolis, discussing a point of contention. Aristotle claims that men should rule and be ruled alike, though non-Greeks are best ruled by a superior Greek king. Alexander considers the best course for one who would rule all.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10113B_NAME">
            <Text>There are Greeks and there are barbarians.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10113B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on the Acropolis.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10113C_NAME">
            <Text>All peoples live and die alike.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10113C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} in Settlements Captured this Age.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10114A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>King of Revelers</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10114A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>So this Xerxes then is the lavish and decadent ruler who claims kingship over a host of barbarians. He seems concerned more with his attire than his defense, with his crown than his kingdom. Alexander had hoped to find a worthy foe.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10114B_NAME">
            <Text>Xerxes will soon witness {1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} strength.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10114B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10114C_NAME">
            <Text>Fine garments are for those who lack wisdom.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10114C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10114D_NAME">
            <Text>Such men rarely inspire loyalty.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10114D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1280A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>To Be a Hero</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1280A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Alexander listens as a bard recites the story of the great Achilles so beloved of the gods. His might, his rage - that most-feared warrior who stalked the fields of Troy. Yet too, he did sing and grieve for Patroclus, and the sweet fate of long life tempted even him.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1280B_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>To Be a Hero</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1280B_NAME">
            <Text>He was a hero because of his valor.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1280B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1280B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The gods reward the mighty.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1280B_IMPERATIVE">
            <Text>Have a Commander with 3 Promotions.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1280C_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>To Be a Hero</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1280C_NAME">
            <Text>The gods love those who bring them gifts.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1280C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1280C_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The gods' blessings are known to all.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1280C_IMPERATIVE">
            <Text>Have 3 Altars.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1280D_NAME">
            <Text>Heroes of the past are tales for children.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1280D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1281A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Making of a Name</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1281A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Across the battlefield, Alexander charges, first in line to strike terror in the enemy's hearts. One by one they fall, the few survivors carrying word of the great king and his overwhelming might. A tremor of fear ripples across the landscape.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1281B_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Making of a Name</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1281B_NAME">
            <Text>Claim their land. The gods will it.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1281B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1281B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The taste of victory awakens a thirst for conquest.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1281B_IMPERATIVE">
            <Text>Capture a Settlement you did not Found.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1281C_NAME">
            <Text>Coin can calm a raging heart. Temporarily.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1281C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1282A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Festival of the Muses</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1282A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Musicians, actors, and bards are gathered in {1_capital}, ready to compete for the prize awarded to the most talented. The city is full of eager spectators, enchanted by the many tales and songs that feature Alexander himself.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1282B_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Festival of the Muses</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1282B_NAME">
            <Text>Create a permanent position dedicated to the Muses.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1282B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1282B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The fame of Alexander grows.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1282B_IMPERATIVE">
            <Text>Have 2 Specialists on Culture Buildings.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1282C_NAME">
            <Text>Take a bow with the actors.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1282C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10115A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Fate of Decadence</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10115A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The ground hums with the march of Alexander’s soldiers as they cascade through the fallen capital. Xerxes’ grand palace stands at the city center, waiting to accept its fate.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10115B_NAME">
            <Text>Loot the treasure and leave it to rot.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10115B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}, but {2_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10115C_NAME">
            <Text>Burn away the stench of Xerxes.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10115C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}, but a random Constructible in {2_STORY_CITY} is Pillaged.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10115D_NAME">
            <Text>Dedicate the building to {1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} gods.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10115D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>A Great Work slot is added to {1_STORY_CITY}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10116A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>A Man’s Best Friend</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10116A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Long has Bucephalus, Alexander’s trusted horse, accompanied him in battle. Together, they have fought and conquered. But now, he lies prone, mortally wounded, and the physician shakes his head mournfully. How can a man withstand such grief!</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10116B_NAME">
            <Text>Host a grand funeral for the greatest of companions.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10116B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} and {2_reward} on all Units.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10116C_NAME">
            <Text>Celebrate his well-lived life with a feast.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10116C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} and +10% [icon:GROWTH_RATE] Growth Rate in Settlements.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10117A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>A Knot’s Tale</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10117A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Within the borders of Alexander’s new city, an old oxcart is tied with an impossible knot. Legend says that whoever can loosen the knot and untie the cart will rule the continent.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10117B_NAME">
            <Text>Slice the knot in half. That will loosen it.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10117B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10117C_NAME">
            <Text>Remove the cart’s yoke to reveal the rope’s ends.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10117C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10118A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>A Riddle for the Gymnosophists</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10118A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>A group of gymnosophists live in this region, and Alexander is eager to hear how their notions differ from those of {1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} philosophers. One of the naked ascetics proposes a riddle contest. It seems matching wits is popular everywhere.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10118B_NAME">
            <Text>What came first - night or day?</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10118B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Story continues.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10118C_NAME">
            <Text>Which is stronger - life or death?</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10118C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Story continues.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10118D_NAME">
            <Text>Conquest leaves no time for riddles.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10118D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} in {2_capital}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10119A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>A Riddle for the Gymnosophists</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10119A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>“Day came first, of course, by exactly one night,” answers the first gymnosophist. “Nonsense,” claims another, “night came first, by exactly one day.” Alexander shakes his head and asks another question.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10119B_NAME">
            <Text>How can a man become a god?</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10119B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Story continues.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10119C_NAME">
            <Text>How long is a life well-lived?</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10119C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Story continues.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10120A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>A Riddle for the Gymnosophists</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10120A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The ascetic speaks quietly. “The dead are countless, yet invisible. Life is stronger as it holds all their miseries.” Another ponders, “Life is like the sun - strong at its height, then weaker as it falls and ultimately fades away.” Satisfied, Alexander asks another.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10120B_NAME">
            <Text>What is the wisest of animals?</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10120B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Story continues.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10120C_NAME">
            <Text>What is the cruelest of beasts?</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10120C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Story continues.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10121A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>A Riddle for the Gymnosophists</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10121A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>A lively debate has followed Alexander’s question, for none can truly know the measure of man or beast. The gymnosophists eye him with interest, eager to ask their own. “Tell us, King Alexander, what should a man do to be most loved?”</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10121B_NAME">
            <Text>Seek power yet cause no fear.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10121B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10121C_NAME">
            <Text>Enforce justice with the sword.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10121C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10122A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Unity of Mankind</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10122A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Alexander's realm incorporates cities that once birthed civilizations. Their people hold customs that sometimes ignite polemics from more conservative citizens. While some worship kings as gods, others claim all men are equal.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10122B_NAME">
            <Text>{1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} culture will unite the world.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10122B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>+1 [icon:YIELD_CULTURE] Culture on Specialists.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10122C_NAME">
            <Text>Kings stand far above the common man.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10122C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>+2 Promotions to Highest Level Commander.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1283A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>How to Rule the World</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1283A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Word has begun to spread that Alexander is blessed by the gods. Enemy lances slide past him, and the sky itself keeps arrows from his skin. The songs they sing of him please even the Muses.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1283B_NAME">
            <Text>Conquest is the only way to rule the world.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1283B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Story continues.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1283C_NAME">
            <Text>Poetry and song will make the world ask to be ours.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1283C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Story continues.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1284A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>To the Shores of Oceanus</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1284A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>New lands and new kings inspire Alexander to press further. The bounds of his kingdom shall be the bounds of the world. Nothing less suits a hero.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1284B_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>To the Shores of Oceanus</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1284B_NAME">
            <Text>Onward! Glory awaits.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1284B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1284B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The Muses watch from afar as the world changes hands.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1284B_IMPERATIVE">
            <Text>Capture 2 Settlements in Distant Lands.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1284C_NAME">
            <Text>War is all and good, but a little coin never hurt.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1284C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1285A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>A Rival Champion</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1285A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Recently, Alexander has heard his men speak of one of the enemy’s commanders. Hailing from the far continent, this general uses tactics never before seen. Facing him will be a worthy challenge.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1285B_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>A Rival Champion</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1285B_NAME">
            <Text>A charge from the right flank will unsettle him.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1285B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} on Cavalry Units.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1285B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>{1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} horse are fearsome indeed.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1285B_IMPERATIVE">
            <Text>Defeat an Army Commander in Distant Lands.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1286A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Capture Them with Culture</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1286A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Alexander's new city glistens with promise, but some of the locals greet their new lord with skepticism. Urban amenities will showcase the benefits of his rule, but a grander display would remove any lingering doubt.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1286B_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Capture Them with Culture</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1286B_NAME">
            <Text>Construct something the world has never seen.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1286B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1286B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Stories of {1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} splendor spread further.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1286B_IMPERATIVE">
            <Text>Build a Wonder in Distant Lands.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1286C_NAME">
            <Text>Coin can change minds just as easily.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1286C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1287A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Only the Truth</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1287A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>An envoy from a neighboring town has come offering gifts to Alexander and to the {1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} people. Though he has heard of the grandeur of Alexander’s cities, seeing it in truth stikes him speechless. Cities are for men, but this shines as for a god.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1287B_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Only the Truth</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1287B_NAME">
            <Text>Mention the many positions open for talented souls.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1287B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>+1 [icon:YIELD_CULTURE] Culture on Specialists.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1287B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>All are welcome in {1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} cities.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1287B_IMPERATIVE">
            <Text>Have 10 Specialists in Distant Lands.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10123A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>The Gift of Self-Government</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10123A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Some kings rule by enforcing a uniformity of thought, but in Alexander’s mind, self-government is a reward for discipline. Noble minds have no need to be yoked by the collar of might.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10123B_NAME">
            <Text>Free citizens strengthen the state.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10123B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10123C_NAME">
            <Text>Hegemony need not require force.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10123C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>+3 [icon:YIELD_CULTURE] Culture per Suzerained City-State.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10124A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>Hard Questions and Hard Answers</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10124A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Two friends are playing chess in the park, but the game captures the least of their attention. They bicker colorfully about an old riddle - what is the greatest extent of man? Finally, one stands and exclaims her answer. The other softly says, “Checkmate.”</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10124B_NAME">
            <Text>Do something no mortal can.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10124B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10124C_NAME">
            <Text>A noble death ends a virtuous life.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10124C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10124D_NAME">
            <Text>Man is the most cunning of beasts.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10124D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Gain the earliest available Technology.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10124E_NAME">
            <Text>Of all creatures, man is the most wicked.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_10124E_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>+1 Resource Slot in Settlements with a Factory.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1288A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>King of the World</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1288A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>Each morning, Alexander wakes to yet still more of the world beyond his grasp. The horizon taunts him with lands not his own. His thirst for conquest will be sated.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1288B_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>King of the World</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1288B_NAME">
            <Text>Show the world its rightful ruler.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1288B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_child_reward}</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1288B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>The edge of the world is so close now.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1288B_IMPERATIVE">
            <Text>Capture a Capital.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1288C_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1288C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1288D_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1288D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} and enter a Celebration.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1289A_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>An Epic Hero</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1289A_COMPLETION">
            <Text>{1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ: gender *:an?An; other?A;} {1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} composer has captured the nation’s imagination with their latest work - an opera that features the legend of Alexander, godlike hero, greatest of all men. Citizens and tourists alike are inspired to learn more of his exploits.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1289B_STORYTITLE">
            <Text>An Epic Hero</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1289B_NAME">
            <Text>Promote the work of {1_CIVILIZATION_ADJ} archaeologists.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1289B_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_child_reward}</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1289B_COMPLETION">
            <Text>History and legend are now one.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1289B_IMPERATIVE">
            <Text>Have 6 Displayed Artifacts.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1289C_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1289C_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward}.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1289D_NAME">
            <Text>Close.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_LEADER_CHAIN_1289D_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>{1_reward} and enter a Celebration.</Text>
        </Row>
    </EnglishText>
